          <declname>interval</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Schedule Table. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Register a table for periodic background retention enforcement.</para>
<para>The scheduler runs in a dedicated thread. Each registered table is checked every <computeroutput>interval</computeroutput> and the previously-registered policy (setPolicy) is applied. The table pointer must remain valid until <ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1RetentionManager_1acbc98e447b9d35f8e851e0c5a6b67dd4" kindref="member">stopScheduler()</ref> or the <ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1RetentionManager" kindref="compound">RetentionManager</ref> is destroyed.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>table</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Reference to the table to maintain. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>interval</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>How often to enforce the policy (minimum 1 millisecond).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Call <ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1RetentionManager_1a2f4e1a4a28c7879d5aff64a83b30631c" kindref="member">startScheduler()</ref> once to activate background processing.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">table</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input/output parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">interval</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Calls: lock(), std::chrono::milliseconds(), std::chrono::steady_clock::now(), push_back(), std::move(). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
