    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1RetentionManager" kindref="compound">RetentionManager</ref></para>
<para>Applies retention policies to <ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1SystemVersionedTable" kindref="compound">SystemVersionedTable</ref> instances to enforce data-lifecycle requirements. Archived versions are kept in an in-memory archive for the duration of the process; in production these would be written to cold storage.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1RetentionManager_1a0b68edd9f880964928ae49587cae0e98" kindref="member">enforceRetention()</ref></computeroutput> physically removes historical versions that violate the policy via <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1SystemVersionedTable_1ae4ac8203c11c42a5f08abba67c25f90e" kindref="member">SystemVersionedTable::purgeHistoricalVersions()</ref></computeroutput>. The current (live) row is never removed. If <computeroutput>archive_before_delete</computeroutput> is set, a copy is placed in the in-memory archive before deletion.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para><bold>Deleted-key coverage</bold>: <computeroutput>getAllKeys()</computeroutput> is used so that even fully- deleted keys (no current row) are included in the retention scan.</para>
</simplesect>
Thread-safety: all public methods are thread-safe. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
